From 824f80b944892fb9c417502a7978ab8162077fcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 13:23:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Epic 7B.1: OrgUnit Foundation (ADR-012)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the OrgUnit aggregate — the recursive, single-parent, typed
organizational node — as the foundation of the Organization domain. No
Assignment, Location, or LegalEntity (deferred per ADR-012).

Aggregate & hierarchy:
- One typed OrgUnit (kind in DIVISION/BUSINESS_UNIT/DEPARTMENT/BRANCH/TEAM),
  never a table per level. Strict single-parent tree; pure helpers for tree
  building, descendant collection, and cycle detection.
- Immutable id + code, no hard delete (archive only) — IDs never reused.

Persistence & integrity:
- Prisma OrgUnit model + migration. Tenant isolation is enforced at the DB by
  a composite (tenant_id, parent_id) -> (tenant_id, org_unit_id) foreign key,
  so a parent can never be cross-tenant. CHECK constraints for valid kind,
  valid status, and no self-parent; unique (tenant, code).
- Read + write repository ports with Prisma and in-memory implementations;
  reads require organization.view.

Write path (audit + outbox reused):
- OrgUnit write-transaction buffers one domain event per mutation; a
  PrismaOrgUnitUnitOfWork (mirroring the configuration UoW) commits the unit,
  audit record, and outbox message atomically. Additive
  AuditRecordFactory.organizationEvent. A single OrgUnitService owns the
  structural invariants enforced in-transaction — unique code, parent
  existence, and cycle prevention — gated by a new organization.manage
  permission.

Also folds the three role->permission derivations (hasPermission, production,
development) onto one source of truth (permissionsForRoles) so new permissions
no longer need three edits.

Architecture fitness: registry-style import rules protecting the read-only
read model, the peer-domain boundary (Configuration and Organization must not
couple), and client isolation; plus a structural test asserting a single
OrgUnit aggregate and single hierarchy implementation.

Tests: +31 (aggregate/validation/tree/cycle, service permission/audit/outbox/
cycle/tenant-isolation/rollback, structure, and a real-DB integration test for
atomic audit+outbox, DB guards, hierarchy, and tenant isolation). Full suite
358 unit + 15 integration green; lint, typecheck, build, fitness pass.

